        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "579dc0ee-43ac-5b99-a2e6-5cf9873ec1ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jamie Bell, Steven Gould, Ed Whitmore\n- Works: Billy Elliot, King Kong, Jumper, The Adventures of Tintin, Snowpiercer, Hallam Foe, Turn\n- Topics: film adaptations, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Andrew James Matfin Bell was born on 14 March 1986 and is an English actor and dancer.\n- Jamie Bell rose to prominence for his debut role in \"Billy Elliot\" (2000), which won him the BAFTA for Best Actor in a Leading Role.\n- The novel \"Hallam Foe\" was published on August 11, 2001.\n- \"Jumper\" is a 2008 American science fiction action film loosely based on Steven Gould's 1992 science fiction novel of the same name.\n- \"Hallam Foe\" inspired a film adaptation of the same name by Ed Whitmore starring Jamie Bell, and the film was released in the UK on August 31, 2007.\n- Jamie Bell is also known for roles in \"King Kong\" (2005), \"Jumper\" (2008), \"The Adventures of Tintin\" (2011), and \"Snowpiercer\" (2013).\n- Jamie Bell starred as Abraham Woodhull in the TV series \"Turn\" beginning in 2014.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
